    "result_text": "The full suite is green. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes along with a successful build.\n\nHere's a summary of the change I implemented so the create endpoint returns `namesakeCount` = the number of existing owners (before this create) sharing the same `firstName` and `lastName`, case-insensitively:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `namesakeCount` (int32, min 0) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains a `namesakeCount` field (MapStruct maps it by name automatically).\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persistent `namesakeCount` field (`namesake_count` column) with getter/setter, so the value computed at create time is stored and returned on later `GET`s.\n- **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `namesake_count` column to the `owners` table.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Before saving, sets `namesakeCount` via a new helper that streams `findAllOwners()` and counts those whose first and last names match (case-insensitively) the owner being created. Since it runs before the new owner is persisted, a unique name yields `0`; the test's second `Ann Sur\u2026` owner correctly sees `1`.",
